tion, beats everything.\n        13. Quadplex set: a quad with two single cards OR two pairs attached.\n        Use the EXACT card symbols provided in the Valid Moves list.\n        Prepare a valid JSON object like {"cards": ["♠3", "♥3"]} for your answer, along with your explanation and reason. If you pass, output: {"cards": []}\n        \n        Now is your turn, to your best ability, choose your move to maximize your chances of winning.\n        Please briefly evaluate a few proimsing moves, provide reason for your final choice, and output the action with specified format.\n        Your response format should be:\n        Evaluation: [Your Evaluation]\n        Reason: [Your Reason]\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\n    ', 'user_prompt': "You are playing as the landlord. The landlord's aim is to be the first to play out all his cards in valid combinations. If any of the other players manages to play all their cards before the landlord, you lose.\nYou are the Landlord. Both the Next Player (Right) and the Previous Player (Left) are Peasants and are your ENEMIES. You fight alone. The objective is to empty your hand as fast as possible.\n\nYour Hand: ♥4 ♣4 ♦4 ♠8 ♥8 ♠10 ♥10 ♦10 ♣J ♦J ♠Q ♣Q ♠2\nLast Play to Beat: ♦5\n--- Game History (Recent) ---\nTurn 3 (You): ♦K\nTurn 4 (Next Player): ♥2\nTurn 4 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 4 (You): Pass\nTurn 5 (Next Player): ♥7\nTurn 5 (Prev Player): ♥J\nTurn 5 (You): ♣2\nTurn 6 (Next Player): RedJoker\nTurn 6 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 6 (You): Pass\nTurn 7 (Next Player): ♥3 ♠4 ♥5 ♣6 ♦7\nTurn 7 (Prev Player): ♣5 ♥6 ♣7 ♦8 ♣9\nTurn 7 (You): Pass\nTurn 8 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 8 (Prev Player): ♦5\n--- Player Info ---\nCards Held by Next Player (Right) [Peasant (Opponent)]: 9\nCards Held by Prev Player (Left) [Peasant (Opponent)]: 4\n--- Cards Remaining Unknown (Card Counting) ---\n(Format explanation: 'Rank: Count', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\nBlackJoker: 1, 2: 1, A: 3, K: 2, Q: 1, 9: 2, 6: 1, 3: 2\nValid Moves:\